# MeroSign needs NO environment variables to run. This file documents the two
# overrides that exist, both optional, and exists mostly to say what is NOT here.
#
# ⚠️ REMOVED, and do not put them back:
#
#   VITE_APPLICATION_ID   an ApplicationId is `hash(package, signer)`, so it is
#                         assigned PER INSTALL and is correct only on the machine
#                         it was copied from. A stale one makes context creation
#                         fail with an opaque 500 that never mentions application
#                         ids. The node is asked instead, matching on the package
#                         below — see `src/lib/appId.ts`.
#   VITE_APPLICATION_PATH pointed at `mero_sign_test_v3.wasm` on a dev S3 bucket:
#                         not the bundle this repo builds, and not the one the
#                         registry publishes.
#   VITE_CONTEXT_ID       a baked context is not something this app can assume
#                         exists on somebody else's node. It had no consumers.

# The reverse-DNS package id. Must match `[package.metadata.calimero].package`
# in `logic/Cargo.toml`; the registry lookup, the deep-link slug and the login
# callback check all key off this exact string. Defaults to the value below.
# VITE_PACKAGE_NAME="com.calimero.mero-sign"

# The registry to resolve that package against. Defaults to the fleet default.
# VITE_REGISTRY_URL="https://apps.calimero.network"
